updater: prereleases for beta channels (Updater.SetPrereleases)

Apps updated from GitHub read releases/latest/download/update-<target>.json,
and GitHub's latest release is never a prerelease, so there was no way to
ship a beta to the users who want one. mygo.Updater.SetPrereleases(true),
which the app sets from its own preference (a beta channel), makes Check
find the newest version among releases and prereleases instead:

- internal/update: ResolvePrereleaseFeed lists the releases through the
  GitHub API (the pages and limits of the tagged feeds), skips drafts, and
  takes the highest version (Compare) of the first page that has any, so a
  fix of an older version published later does not hide a newer
  prerelease. Feeds of the latest release use the tags of `mygo build`
  (v{version}); tagged feeds keep to their prefix; other feeds are their
  manifest. update.GitHub is the site, which tests replace, like GitHubAPI.
- Check reads the manifest in the release found, so signatures and deltas
  work as before. When the API fails (60 requests an hour without a token),
  it reads the latest release instead, and fails with the API's error when
  there is none. Turning prereleases off never offers an older version.
- The updater plugin's window and background checks call Updater.Check,
  so they follow the setting.
- `mygo build -upload` creates the draft of a prerelease version
  (update.IsPrerelease) with --prerelease, so publishing it leaves the
  latest release alone.
- Delta updates on GitHub: the build makes them from the newest versions
  of the latest release's manifest and of the newest prerelease's,
  together, so 1.3.0-beta.2 has a delta from 1.3.0-beta.1, and 1.3.0 from
  both the betas and 1.2.x. When the prerelease lookup fails, the build
  warns and keeps the latest release's.

Tests: TestResolvePrereleaseFeed (fake API: prerelease newer or older than
the release, drafts, by version not date, tagged pages, failures, other
feeds), TestUpdaterPrereleases (check from either channel, no downgrade,
install of the prerelease from its delta, API failure fallback, a
repository with only prereleases), TestWriteDeltasPrereleases,
TestPublishGitHub (--prerelease), TestIsPrerelease.
