+## Prereleases
+
+A version such as `1.3.0-beta.1` is a prerelease: `Compare` orders it
+before `1.3.0`, and on GitHub `mygo build -upload` makes its draft a
+prerelease, which never becomes the latest release. Apps that only take
+releases never see it; those whose users joined a beta channel do:
+
+```go
+// At every launch, before the first check, from the app's settings.
+mygo.Updater.SetPrereleases(settings.Beta)
+```
+
+With `SetPrereleases(true)`, `Check` finds the newest version on GitHub,
+prerelease or release, through the GitHub API (one request a check), and
+reads the manifest of its release. A release newer than the prereleases,
+such as `1.3.0` after `1.3.0-beta.2`, is offered too. When the API fails,
+for example past its 60 requests an hour for each address, `Check` reads
+the latest release instead. Turning prereleases off never offers an older
+version: an app on `1.3.0-beta.2` stays there until a release newer than
+it, `1.3.0`, is out.
+
+Updates from a `url` have a single manifest, which apps read either way:
+serve prereleases to beta testers from a build of their own, with another
+`url`.
+
+Delta updates follow both: on GitHub, `mygo build` makes them from the
+newest versions of the latest release's manifest and of the newest
+prerelease's, together, so the next prerelease updates the one before with
+a delta, and the release updates both the prereleases and the releases
+before it.
+
+Changelog sections are found by the exact version: `## 1.3.0-beta.1`.
+
